            "title": "RedisClient constructor mishandles undefined options argument",
            "severity": "high",
            "file": "index.js",
            "line": 39,
            "explanation": "The original code calls JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(options)) without providing a default for options. If options is undefined, this throws an error. The patch fixes this by using options || {}, ensuring options is at least an empty object before serialization and parsing.",
            "suggestion": "Change line 39 from `options = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(options));` to `options = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(options || {}));` to safely handle missing options argument."
